# No em dashes

Do **not** use the Unicode em dash (U+2014). Prefer a hyphen with spaces (` - `), a colon, parentheses, or a new sentence.

## Applies to

- Markdown docs (`README.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md`, `SETUP_GUIDE.md`, `DEMO_SCRIPT.md`, root guides)
- Catalog and detail copy (`_data/demos.yml`, `_data/demo_pages.yml`, `_data/demo_playbooks.yml`, `_data/ao_glossary.yml`)
- Contribute / Pages HTML prose
- Cursor rules (`.cursor/rules/*.mdc`) and assistant guides (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`)

## Prefer instead

| Bad pattern | Good alternatives |
|---|---|
| clause [em dash] clause | `clause - clause` |
| Title [em dash] subtitle | `Title: subtitle` or `Title - subtitle` |
| aside [em dash] note | `aside (note)` or a new sentence |

## Examples

**Incorrect:** `Approve when prompted` then an em dash then `watch OpenFlake.`  
**Correct:** `Approve when prompted - then watch OpenFlake.`

**Incorrect:** `Demo walkthrough` then an em dash then `happy path`  
**Correct:** `Demo walkthrough - happy path`

When editing existing files, replace any em dashes you touch. Do not introduce new ones.
